course: dictionary
lesson: 2196
title: One word, many meanings: cough
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which is its context. «Cough» can be something a person does, a sound, an illness, or a noise from a machine, so check the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: To cough is to push air out of your lungs suddenly with a loud noise, often because something is in your throat or you are ill. «If someone is choking and cannot talk or cough, get an adult at once.» Here cough is the action your body does to clear your airways.
explain: A cough can also be a noun, meaning the action, the sound or an illness. «A chesty cough, body aches or a tummy bug are «below the neck» signs.» Here a cough is an illness. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Machines can cough too. When an engine coughs, it makes a rough, broken sound. Phrases like «cough up» are informal and can mean pay or give, so always look at the clues.
fact: To cough means to push air out of your lungs suddenly with a loud noise.
fact: A cough is the body clearing its airways, often when something is in your throat.
fact: Coughs and sneezes spread germs, so cover them with a tissue or your elbow.
fact: Throw the tissue away and wash your hands, so germs do not spread.
fact: A cough that lasts weeks, or comes with trouble breathing, needs a doctor.
exercise: «Colds and flu are caused by viruses, tiny germs that travel in the drops we sneeze and cough out.» In this sentence, what does cough mean? | *To push air out of your lungs suddenly with a loud noise | A machine that makes a rough sound | A bad cold that lasts a week | A medicine for coughs
exercise: «A chesty cough, body aches or a tummy bug are «below the neck» signs.» In this sentence, what is a cough? | A way of covering your mouth | *An illness that makes you cough a lot | A rough sound from an engine | To push air out loudly
exercise: Ella says her dad's old van coughs every time he starts it. What does coughs mean here? | Is ill with a bad cold | *Makes a rough, broken sound | Pays money to the garage | Gives a loud sneeze
test: «Covering a cough» stops germs spreading. What does cough mean here? | A medicine that stops germs | *The action or sound of pushing air out of your lungs | A tissue used to wipe your nose | A machine's rough noise
test: What is whooping cough? | A loud bird song | *An illness that makes you cough a lot | A machine that clears the air | A soft, quiet whisper
exam: «A cough that lasts weeks or comes with trouble breathing needs a doctor.» What should you do if a cough lasts weeks? | Ignore it, because coughs always stop | Shake the cough out of your chest | Use a cough sweet and wait | *Tell a doctor or an adult
